# (do not ignore docs/claim-locks/)
# Heavy edition PDFs / dumps — keep *_source.json locks in git; fetch PDFs via sources/manifest.json
# Large PDFs — keep local only
# Local claim locks are created by `claims.py take` — commit them when claiming so remotes see the lock
books/**/sources/*_djvu.txt
books/**/sources/pg12_epub/
books/**/sources/pg12*.epub
books/origen-principiis/sources/koetschau_gcs22_djvu.txt
books/origen-psalms-rufinus/sources/*.pdf
books/origen-romans/sources/*_djvu.txt
books/origen-romans/sources/*.pdf
outputs/*
# ...except durable cross-agent ledgers (upload record, triage queues).
!outputs/logos_uploads.json
!outputs/edition-backfill-*.json
!outputs/lineage-triage-*.json
venv/
books/origen-luke-homilies/sources/rauer_gcs35_djvu.txt
books/**/sources/*.png
books/**/sources/*.jpg
books/**/sources/bekker-pages/

# OCR page images are derived from the source PDFs (fetched via
# sources/manifest.json); keep the text locks in git, not GBs of scans
# (2026-10-03: 274 new pages, ~2 GB, broke pushes). Already-tracked pages stay.
books/**/sources/**/*_ocr/*.png
books/**/sources/**/_ocr*/*.png
books/**/sources/**/*_ocr/*.jpg
books/**/sources/**/_ocr*/*.jpg
